neurs [3] analysing patients from different Dutch databases, LUMINA (migraine) and NESDA (depression and anxiety), using the Mood and Anxiety Questionnaire (MASQ-30) to assess three dimensions -lack of positive affect (depression specific); negative affect (nonspecific); and somatic arousal (anxiety specific), the later being the most important.", "bbox": {"x": 839.6, "y": 1612.3, "width": 661.1999999999999, "height": 428.20000000000005}}], "ms": 361.74}